# 2026-10-21 the control of the YNNPACK CPU rows of matrices/lu1020-q06-cpu-android.cells (lane lu1020, round r1b;
# supervisor 2026-10-20 22:2x): the protocol only (1,024 prompt / 256 decode tokens at context 2,048), six arms in one
# Galaxy S26 sitting, each build's XNNPACK row (arm litert-lm-cpu) and YNNPACK row (ynnpack=1 = --enable_ynnpack=true,
# arm litert-lm-cpu-ynnpack) on one binary:
#   HEAD     = side build head-lm2ef6baeb-rtd469ea48-xnn878f1d8c-ynn-cpuonly, the Hub file
#              Qwen3-0.6B_dynamic_wi4b32_afp32.litertlm (block-32 INT4 weights): the two rows are the protocol rows of
#              matrices/lu1020-q06-cpu-android.cells unchanged, so they are also the S26 retake of those cells.
#   slinkytf = side build head-lm2ef6baeb-rtd469ea48-xnn878f1d8c-ynn-cpuonly-slinkytf (android/engine-pins.json): the
#              same build without its slinky override, slinky at what LiteRT-LM 2ef6baeb's workspace resolves
#              (TensorFlow / XLA a3eec6fc) instead of LiteRT d469ea48's pin 9b2ee975 (slinky 26eddcb5, between the two,
#              raises the Android spin count of slinky's thread pool, which YNNPACK runs on, from 1000 to 10000000), on
#              the same Hub file under the model id ..._ctl_slinkytf: a protocol capture is named by arm, model id and
#              task only (android/bench/run_cell.py capture_stem), so a second build of one cell in one sitting needs
#              its own id or the gate would judge the two builds' records as one capture.
#   int8     = the HEAD build on the Hub's dynamic INT8 file Qwen3-0.6B.litertlm (litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B main
#              e6687177, lfs sha256 c5f39b41…, 613,722,264 B) under its catalog id litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B/dynamic_int8
#              (the iOS and Mac id of the same file): does YNNPACK take the FULLY_CONNECTED weights of an INT8 file,
#              which it refuses in the block-32 INT4 file (dot.cc IsTensorSupported(weights), 339 lines per launch)?
# The payload runs round-robin (run_campaign: each round runs the six rows once, in this order). Not page rows; the
# records tell the builds apart by conditions.engineBuild / engineVersion. First row = the Android session anchor.
#   BENCH_SITTING=1 python3 scripts/dashboard_job.py s26 --cells matrices/lu1020-q06-cpu-ctl-android.cells --suffix lu1020-ctl --once --hold-held-by <keeper pid> --no-page-commit

